--[[
  It all starts with one Forge. A Forge loads the providers of one side,
  the server or the client, runs their `Init` in order, wires their
  lifecycles, and starts them. This tour uses it in every step.

  These files import Forge from `@packages/forge`, where `embr install`
  puts it. A game can also re-export Forge from one module of its own,
  such as `@shared/forge`, and import from there.
]]

import { Forge } from '@packages/forge'

-- The main script of a side does one thing: it sets up Forge. Each child
-- of the `Providers` folder is a provider module. Step 002 writes one.
new Forge()
  :AddProviders(script.Parent->'Providers'!:GetChildren())
  :Start()

--[[
  `new Forge(options?)` takes `{ Verbose = false }` to turn off the boot
  summary that Forge prints:

    Forge (Server) started 6 providers in 4ms

  Each `Add` call returns the Forge, so the calls chain. `Start` runs the
  boot once. A second `Start`, or an `Add` after it, errors with
  `BadCall:`.
]]
